zune-jpeg: validate the vertical up-sampling geometry before the row carry-over

worker.rs `upsample()` (V/HV ratios) rejects a component whose `raw_coeff`
is not a whole number of `width_stride * vertical_sample` rows ("Invalid
component dimensions, would panic"), but only after it has up-sampled the
carried-over last row of the previous MCU row for `i > 0`. A one-shot decode
always reaches the check on MCU row 0 first; an incremental decode that
resumes at a later MCU row (here after a multi-SOS stream changed the scan
layout) skipped it and called the up-sampler with mismatched slices, which
panics on its length assertions (scalar.rs:59/81, avx2.rs:100/183). Do the
check before the carry-over as well; behaviour for valid images is unchanged.
Includes a regression test (tests/incremental_resume.rs).

Not fixed upstream as of zune-image 2cdbbf5.
Upstream: related open issue #236 (assertion `left == right` failed in the
up-sampler, one-shot path); none found for the resumed path.

